{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Whosoever offers his offering.</b> After speaking of the priests who offer and of their sanctity, he speaks of the conditions of the offerings themselves and says <b>for all their vows and for all their freewill offerings.</b> For even though they are voluntary offerings, one might suppose that whatever one vows — even a blemished animal — would be acceptable, since no obligation was imposed upon him, as some of Israel supposed. The prophet exposed their error, saying: וְכִי תַגִּישׁוּן עִוֵּר לִזְבֹּחַ אֵין רָע, וְכִי תַגִּישׁוּ פִּסֵּחַ וְחֹלֶה אֵין רָע, הַקְרִיבֵהוּ נָא לְפֶחָתֶךָ (Malachi 1:8)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:29.048109504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}